Description: Window menu requests and ping/pong for the server
 xdg_toplevel.show_window_menu and xdg_wm_base.pong were empty TODO stubs.
 The server can now show its window menu when a client asks (right-click on
 a client-side title bar): Mir looks up mir_show_window_menu_hook in the
 executable and calls it on the Wayland thread with the window's
 scene::Surface and the surface-local position. For "App is not
 responding", Mir hands the function mir_xdg_ping_setup_hook a function that
 pings every xdg_wm_base of a process (on the Wayland thread), and passes
 each pong to mir_xdg_pong_hook with the client's pid. A server without the
 hooks behaves as before. No ABI change.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: not yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-16
---
